[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ipni-maturity-iteration-01", :doc/title "IPNI maturity — Co-Scientist iteration 01", :doc/path "90-docs/ipni_maturity/iteration-01.edn", :source/dataset "ipni-maturity", :doc/measured-at "2026-08-20T06:12:57Z", :doc/score 40.74074074074073, :doc/body "# IPNI maturity — Co-Scientist iteration 01\n\n> Judge: `ipni-maturity.audit` over `ipni-maturity.probe` — measured HTTP\n> statuses and manifest facts, no LLM. Ranking: `kaizen.elo`, round-robin,\n> the measured gain is the judge.\n>\n> Probed 2026-08-20T06:12:57Z. 100.00% of the rubric was measurable; nothing was unmeasurable, so nothing is excluded.\n\n## Score\n\n**40.74 / 100**\n\n## Findings (heaviest recoverable headroom first)\n\n| axis | weight | finding |\n|---|---|---|\n| `discoverable-as-provider` | 0.2 | a CID kotobase serves resolves to third-party providers only — kotobase is not among them |\n| `chain-published` | 0.18 | no advertisement chain has ever been published — /ipni/v1/head is 404 |\n| `advertise-wired` | 0.15 | zero call sites for ipni.advertise/announce/ad/head anywhere in the workspace |\n| `dependency-declared` | 0.08 | io-ipni-specs is not a declared dependency of anything — the library is unreachable from any deployed code |\n| `entries-hamt` | 0.03 | ipni.hamt returns :not-yet-implemented — honest, but caps an advertisement at one EntryChunk |\n\n## Roadmap (Elo)\n\n| Elo | id | axis | startable? | observable? | +gain |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1260 | `ipni-h1` | `discoverable-as-provider` | no — publisher identity (a peer ID) and the advertisement signature | yes | +18.52 |\n| 1230 | `ipni-h2` | `chain-published` | no — publisher identity (a peer ID) and the advertisement signature | yes | +16.67 |\n| 1200 | `ipni-h3` | `advertise-wired` | no — an advertisement needs a signed Provider, so the drain cannot be finished before the identity exists | yes | +13.89 |\n| 1170 | `ipni-h4` | `dependency-declared` | yes | no | +7.41 |\n| 1140 | `ipni-h5` | `entries-hamt` | yes | no | +2.78 |\n\n## Meta\n\n**Every member of the startable batch is unobservable from outside.**\n\nShipping all of it moves the score **+7.41** (to 48.15 / 100) without changing anything a\nstranger can see. That is the same defect as an unmeasured metric wearing the\nopposite mask, so this iteration does not bank the gain: it reports the blocked\nwork instead.\n\nThe three highest-Elo hypotheses share one blocker:\n\n- publisher identity (a peer ID) and the advertisement signature\n- an advertisement needs a signed Provider, so the drain cannot be finished before the identity exists\n\nThat is a decision, not a task. Until it is made, IPNI maturity is capped at 48.15 / 100 and every point of the remainder is behind it.\n\n## Method note\n\nThree earlier versions of the probe swept `orgs/` directly for call sites; on 4,400\ncheckouts none finished, and each reported the two heaviest axes as `:unknown`. The\nworking version derives them instead: a namespace cannot be required without its\ndependency on the classpath, so zero declarations across 4217 repos (3479 manifests read) implies zero call\nsites. The evidence floor is reported so 0 hits cannot be read as 0 looked at.\n"}]